### 3. Additional context (if relevant):
Decisions were made conservatively following the protocol. Studies were excluded if they were not RCTs, had follow-up <6
months, targeted populations outside the 6-11 age range, were protocols/reviews/editorials, or focused on prevention 
rather than treatment. Long-term follow-up reports of eligible RCTs were included to capture sustained outcomes.

Key exclusion reasons:
- Follow-up <6 months: 22 studies
- Not RCTs (quasi-experimental, observational, pretest-posttest): 15 studies
- Protocol/design papers without results: 8 studies
- Systematic reviews/methodological papers: 10 studies
- Population outside age range (preschoolers, adolescents): 5 studies
- Prevention-focused rather than treatment: 4 studies
- Secondary analyses: 4 studies
- Other (editorials, process outcomes, unclear design): 6 studies

