EXCLUSION REASONS BREAKDOWN:
- Not an RCT design: Most common exclusion reason
- Follow-up <6 months or unclear: Studies with insufficient follow-up duration
- Age range not 6-11 years: Studies focusing on younger or older children
- Eating disorder focus: Excluded per protocol
- Not focused on overweight/obesity: Studies not targeting obesity
- No relevant intervention: Studies without diet/PA/behavioral components

All decisions were made conservatively - when in doubt, studies were included for further review.


### 3. Additional context (if relevant):

Screening methodology:
1. Each study was evaluated for RCT design (randomized/randomised/controlled trial)
2. Exclusion criteria checked: eating disorders, type 2 diabetes, secondary/syndromic obesity
3. Population criteria: overweight/obese children aged 6-11 years
4. Intervention criteria: diet, physical activity, or behavioral interventions
5. Follow-up criteria: minimum 6 months

Note: Some borderline cases were included conservatively per protocol guidelines.


