│ in the intervention group (3.8%) than in the control group (6.0%, p = 0.018). Remission of overweight and obesity    │
│ did not differ between the groups. Measured water flow of the fountains indicated a sustained use. CONCLUSION A      │
│ simple dietary intervention with the sole focus on the promotion of drinking water effectively reduced the incidence │
│ of overweight among school children."}, {"study_index": 400, "title": "Stage 1 treatment of pediatric overweight and │
│ obesity: a pilot and feasibility randomized controlled trial", "abstract": "BACKGROUND Staged clinical treatment of  │
│ pediatric obesity is recommended, but untested. Understanding the lowest intensity stage\'s effectiveness is         │
│ necessary for future research. METHODS This was a randomized controlled trial of children ages 4 to <9 years.        │
