│ were undertaken at six monthly intervals and a 7-day food and activity diary were issued. RESULTS Over the 2 years   │
│ of the study body mass index (BMI) SDS (z score) fell significantly in the intervention/control (I/C) group, but not │
│ in the control/intervention (C/I) group. The difference between groups was 0.3, which was borderline significant     │
│ (95% confidence interval (95% CI) -0.62 to 0.02, P=0.06) before adjusting for potential confounding factors.         │
│ Thirty-three percent of the I/C group and 12% of the C/I group achieved the target reduction of 0.5 BMI SDS. The I/C │
│ group had a significantly greater reduction in the percentage with a BMI above the 99.6th centile at 24 months       │
│ (P=0.04) and gained 5.7 kg less over the time of the study. There were no significant differences between groups for │
